{"schema_version":1,"architecture_version":3,"workstream_id":"AAYS_21_SLOT_SAFE_PARALLEL_V1","slot_id":"height_difference_3","task_id":"height_difference_3-canonical-api-measurement-20260721-01","continuation_key":"6e8e709b6bad7b9807055e2b8b5de98cd4945ee3dee57825e72ba1b824eadd0f","created_at":"2026-08-01T11:12:00Z","claim_commit_sha":"7c5cade93d31882fd36ea3f891a9c8bde710f995","state":"WCS_SUBSET_SEAM_EDGE_AND_SMALL_SAMPLE_PERCENTILE_STABILITY_GATE_QUALIFIED_RUNTIME_HELD","purpose":"Qualify complete WCS footprint and halo containment, raster seam/overlap identity, NoData edge completeness and small-parcel P05-P95 stability without executing blocked runtime or promoting numeric values.","official_controls":[{"id":"WCS_SUBSET_DOMAIN_AND_HALO_CONTAINMENT","sources":["https://www.ogc.org/standards/wcs/"],"facts":["WCS retrieves geospatial coverages and its core requirements are mandatory for conformant services.","A bounded GetCoverage response is a coverage whose returned domain must be checked against the requested parcel domain rather than inferred from a successful HTTP response.","A request buffer is an implementation choice and must be verified against the returned grid transform and valid-data footprint."],"decision":"Persist requested subset bounds, parcel bounds, halo size, returned grid bounds/transform, valid-data footprint, parcel-to-edge distances and require full parcel plus declared halo containment before measurement."},{"id":"RASTER_SEAM_OVERLAP_AND_SOURCE_PRIORITY","sources":["https://rasterio.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/rasterio.merge.html","https://rasterio.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/rasterio.rio.merge.html"],"facts":["Rasterio merge uses an explicit method such as first, last, min, max, sum or count.","Input order and resolution selection affect overlap results.","NoData and masks determine which source pixels participate."],"decision":"Do not silently mosaic overlapping EA coverages. Record every intersecting source, overlap pixel count, per-source values and masks, source priority policy and seam disagreement statistics; promotion requires one complete source or an explicitly verified equal-overlap mosaic."},{"id":"GDAL_VRT_NODATA_GAPS_AND_GRID_ALIGNMENT","sources":["https://gdal.org/en/stable/programs/gdalbuildvrt.html","https://gdal.org/en/stable/drivers/raster/vrt.html"],"facts":["GDAL VRT source order controls priority in overlaps unless another pixel function is selected.","Areas not covered by any source can read as zero unless NoData or a mask is explicitly configured.","Target-aligned pixels and explicit source/destination rectangles control grid alignment."],"decision":"Persist VRT/mosaic source order, NoData and mask policy, target alignment, uncovered-cell count, seam/gap bitmap hash and reject implicit zero fill, hidden NoData or unrecorded overlap priority."},{"id":"SMALL_SAMPLE_PERCENTILE_METHOD_AND_TAIL_STABILITY","sources":["https://itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/prc/section2/prc262.htm","https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/generated/numpy.percentile.html"],"facts":["Percentile estimates are based on ordered observations and interpolation methods are not universally identical.","For small samples high and low percentiles can collapse to or depend heavily on extreme order statistics.","Different accepted percentile methods can differ particularly for small samples."],"decision":"Pin NumPy method=linear and persist order statistics/ranks. For candidates below a documented stability count, compute leave-one-out and adjacent accepted-method sensitivity; reject promotion when P05-P95 or confidence class changes materially."},{"id":"TAIL_STATISTIC_UNCERTAINTY_AND_DETERMINISTIC_SENSITIVITY","sources":["https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/eda/section3/bootplot.htm","https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/prc/section1/prc14.htm"],"facts":["Confidence intervals quantify uncertainty in sample statistics.","Bootstrap methods can estimate sampling variation where formulas are difficult.","NIST cautions that bootstrap is not appropriate for all statistics, including statistics strongly dependent on distribution tails."],"decision":"Treat ordinary iid bootstrap as supplementary only. Require deterministic leave-one-out, edge-cell removal, one-pixel boundary erosion/dilation and reproducible seeded spatial-block sensitivity; record interval width and return PASS, FAIL or INCONCLUSIVE."}],"repository_controls":[{"id":"AAYS_013_WCS_FIXED_BUFFER_AND_COMPLETENESS_GAP","path":"docs/chatgpt_status/topography/shards/height_difference_3/automation/013_fetch_ea_dtm_wcs_for_matches.py","sha":"53c7371701f4f3495a4712b472a3a45f1f4fed12","facts":["The script requests parcel bounds with a fixed 5 metre buffer, validates EPSG:27700, dimensions, nominal resolution and parcel intersection.","It does not require the returned valid-data footprint to contain the whole parcel plus halo, record distance to response edges, or prove that boundary pixels are not NoData."],"decision":"Preserve the pinned fetcher and require a supplementary subset/halo/valid-footprint completeness manifest."},{"id":"AAYS_009_SEAM_AND_SMALL_SAMPLE_STABILITY_GAP","path":"docs/chatgpt_status/topography/shards/height_difference_3/automation/009_sample_ea_dtm_and_os_terrain50.py","sha":"42ac87801263b6b94532c0897dbb5211b79ebeb1","facts":["The script masks intersecting rasters, concatenates finite values and ultimately requires exactly one EA coverage and one Terrain50 tile.","It allows a minimum of four EA cells and computes P05-P95 without leave-one-out, edge-cell, method or spatial-block sensitivity.","It does not persist seam distance, overlap disagreement, uncovered-cell bitmap or parcel-to-valid-data-edge margin."],"decision":"Require a per-candidate seam/edge/completeness and percentile-stability manifest before numeric promotion."}],"quality_checks":[{"index":1,"group":"WCS_SUBSET_DOMAIN_AND_HALO_CONTAINMENT","check":"official_wcs_coverage_contract_bound","result":"PASS"},{"index":2,"group":"WCS_SUBSET